From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Mark the assertion-only locals of matcher_stack.cpp as used

matcher_stack.cpp declares locals that only D_ASSERT() reads (frame_count),
so in a release build, where D_ASSERT() expands to nothing, they are unused
and -Wunused-variable or -Wunused-but-set-variable says so. Each is cast
to void after its declaration, which changes no behavior.

Carried here until upstream takes it; not proposed upstream yet.

---
diff --git a/src/duckdb/src/parser/peg/matcher_stack.cpp b/src/duckdb/src/parser/peg/matcher_stack.cpp
--- a/src/duckdb/src/parser/peg/matcher_stack.cpp
+++ b/src/duckdb/src/parser/peg/matcher_stack.cpp
@@ -142,6 +142,7 @@ MatcherResult MatchStack::ExecuteInternal(const Matcher &matcher, MatchState &st
 	while (!frames.empty()) {
 		auto &frame = *frames.back();
 		auto frame_count = frames.size();
+		(void)frame_count;
 		ExecuteFrame(frame);
 		if (!frame.HasResult()) {
 			D_ASSERT(frames.size() > frame_count);
